==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfʌkˌʌp/|lang=en}} (noun)
* {{IPA|/ˌfʌkˈʌp/|lang=en}} (verb)

===Alternative forms===
* [[fuck-up]] ''(UK, noun)''
* [[fuckup]] ''(US regional, noun)''

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[fuck]] [[up]]}}

# {{context|vulgar|lang=en}} An [[incompetent]] individual; one who errs frequently.
#: ''He is such a '''fuck up'''.''
# {{context|vulgar|lang=en}} A severe mistake.
#: ''That '''fuck up''' cost us the contract.''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|One who can never seem to get anything quite right}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|kämmäri}} {{qualifier|slang}}, {{t|fi|mokailija}} {{qualifier|slang}}, {{t|fi|mogari}} {{qualifier|slang}}, {{t|fi|sähläri}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Polish: {{t|pl|zjeb|m}}, {{t+|pl|pierdoła|f}}
* Russian: {{t+|ru|долбоёб|m|tr=dolbojób|sc=Cyrl}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|fucks up|fucking up|fucked up}}

# {{context|intransitive|slang|mildly vulgar|lang=en}} to make a mistake, to go wrong
#: ''You really '''fucked up''' this time.''
# {{context|transitive|vulgar|lang=en}} to [[botch]] or make a mess of
#: ''I '''fucked up''' question 3 of the exam.''
# {{context|transitive|vulgar|lang=en}} to [[injure]] or [[damage]]
#: ''I '''fucked up''' my knee while running the marathon.''
# {{context|used only in imperative|vulgar|lang=en}} short for ''shut the fuck up''.
#: '''''Fuck up''', mate! I don't want to listen to you!''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|make a mistake}} [[screw up]], [[mess up]]; see also [[Wikisaurus:make a mistake]]
* [[mar]]

